  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 240 PM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nThrough the remainder of the weekend, the upper level ridge is \nexpected to shift further eastward over the Central CONUS, but also \nbecome more squished south as a rather potent trough moves across \nthe Pacific Northwest. The net result will be a return of even \nwarmer and humid conditions through early next week as southwest \nflow persists, with various shortwaves suggested to ride the upper \nridge, ultimately putting Iowa into a more active pattern for \nvarious chances of showers and thunderstorms. With Iowa well into \nthe warm sector, capping looks likely at least on Sunday, keeping \nchances for precipitation rather low (20-30%) until around Monday \nevening/Tuesday when a cold front is suggested to push into Iowa. \nMore specific details are expected to become more clear in the \ncoming days for this time period. Temperatures will generally\ntop out in the upper 80s through the 90s, with central and\nsouthern Iowa reaching near 100 degrees for heat indices Sunday\nand Monday.",
